c{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3caebccd-a111-5c41-885b-601d0e3537ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285359} {:answer/id #uuid "5c49b8ca-6a4c-5d5b-bee0-678ddd9d003c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285633} {:answer/id #uuid "77e0a940-8e6f-54a7-9506-301d4949f5ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285904} {:answer/id #uuid "c96c9e76-bbaf-5ac6-a64e-a08681842df9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(14)" :db/id #edb/